    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1904, the The Pas Indian Band opened a sawmill on Mission Island in the Saskatchewan River, sparking early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sam Waller Museum, housed in the old courthouse downtown, chronicles the town’s rich history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pas lies about 520 kilometres northwest of Winnipeg and just 35 kilometres from the Saskatchewan border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
